A||||13||wayne||coolant servicing||||1||
Z||000000||wayne||04-19-2000||04:09 PM||||I'm sure this has been asked millions of time.<BR>What is the proper way of serving the coolant system.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||04-19-2000||04:27 PM||||I'm sure it would like a silver tray but you most likely mean what is the proper way to fill the system. Fill overflow tank  half way Remove the radiator cap(front compartment) then the cap on the engine. Fill until coolant comes out of the radiator, replace rad cap continue filling at engine until full - replace cap. Run the engine up to operating temp then let it cool completely down. Do this 2-3 times keeping an eye on the overflow tank level. That way all air should be removed from the system. Maybe somebody has an easier way but this works.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wayne||04-19-2000||04:31 PM||||If the system is serviced correctly, should you see any fluid in the block when you pull the thermstat out?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick||04-19-2000||04:49 PM||||<BR>I just changed my thermostat today. The fluid level was up and over the thermostat right up to the cap.<P>Wayne, I bet that <I>nobody</I> has <I>ever</I> asked what you asked. Phil knows what I mean. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||04-19-2000||08:14 PM||||I was told to run engine till warm without the thermostat and the thermostat cap closed to the first click stop ( after re-filling of course) Then top up, replace thermostat and cap , fill overflow , check for leaks , drive , re-check level after a couple of days. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||wayne||04-20-2000||10:35 AM||||Thanks for the input, maybe my problems is that it is not serviced correctly.<P>wayne||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||04-20-2000||12:05 PM||||What are your problems? It's easier to offer solutions if we know what the exact problems are.||||reg||1
Z||000007||wayne||04-20-2000||04:32 PM||||The car is cold at the time of start up.<P>Sometimes (like most Fiero Problems) when you start the car up and drive it usually about a mile or so, it overheats immediately.<P>The temp gage goes up, the car stops, and most of the time water overflows out of the water overflow tank.<P>I've chenged thermostates tried running with and without thermostats. <P>I've pressure check the system to check for blow head gasket or craked head, all OK.<P>The water pump has been changed.<P>You drive the car for weeks and all be of and then all of a sudden it's back.<P>wayne||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dan||04-25-2000||09:29 PM||||Make sure the coolant overflow is topped off.It will take care of itself.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||04-25-2000||09:57 PM||||I believe I got this link from somebody here! <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~fieroshadow/fierohelp/coolant.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.att.net/~fieroshadow/fierohelp/coolant.html</A> ||||reg||1
